+// directory, because declarativeNetRequest writes its index next to the rules
+// and the host's copy may be inside the signed app, and loads them as the
+// static rulesets of a component extension, "ReArc Blocker", in every profile
+// the host has switched blocking on for. Nothing here is the source of truth:
+// the host says which lists, which sites are excepted and which rules are the
+// person's own, at profile load and on every change. A profile the host has
+// said nothing about has no blocker.
