+// There are two such extensions, with two IDs (kContentBlockerExtensionIds),
+// and in ordinary times one of them is loaded. On a list update the new
+// bundle is loaded as the other one, and the old one goes on blocking until
+// the new one's lists are on: an extension cannot change its rulesets'
+// files without a reload, and a reload leaves every open page unblocked
+// while 18,000 rules are indexed (security CB-02).
